; Comment lines beneath a nested account declaration carry metadata for
; the account at their own depth: a comment indented under the nested
; `account` belongs to it, and one back at the outer depth, after the
; nested block, belongs to the enclosing account again.  Assets:Savings,
; never declared, inherits only the enclosing account's tags.  A tab
; counts as one column, so the tab-indented Liabilities block nests the
; same way.

account Assets
    ; Owner: family
    account Checking
        ; Owner: joint
        ; Bank: First
    ; Purpose: spending

account Liabilities
	; Owner: family
	account Card
		; Bank: Second
	; Purpose: credit

2024-01-01 Paycheck
    Assets:Checking    $100.00
    Assets:Savings      $50.00
    Income:Salary

2024-01-02 Groceries
    Expenses:Food    $20.00
    Liabilities:Card

test bal --flat --no-total --balance-format "%(account)|%(tag(\"Owner\"))|%(tag(\"Bank\"))|%(tag(\"Purpose\"))\n" ^Assets ^Liabilities
Assets:Checking|joint|First|spending
Assets:Savings|family||spending
Liabilities:Card|family|Second|credit
end test
